WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:05.340
The Grudge is many things, but subtle ain't
one of 'em so you probably didn't get too

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.570
lost along the way.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:10.950
But just in case, here's everything you need
to know to make sense of The Grudge's shocking

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:11.950
ending.

00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.599
Beware: Spoilers abound!

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:18.980
The Grudge tells its story out of order, saving
the big reveals for when they will deliver

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.010
the biggest emotional punch.

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:25.519
Telling the story chronologically isn't as
interesting, but it is necessary to understand

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:26.519
the ending.

00:00:26.519 --> 00:00:31.760
In 2004, Fiona Landers returns home from Japan,
where she worked as a caretaker in a cursed

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:32.760
house.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:37.160
Unfortunately, while Fiona is happy to be
reunited with her husband Sam and her daughter

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.110
Melinda, the joy doesn't last.

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:44.840
The curse has followed Fiona home to 44 Reyburn
Drive, where, driven mad by the apparitions

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:50.010
she sees, she drowns Melinda and stabs Sam,
then takes her own life.

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:55.120
Shortly afterwards, married real estate agents
Peter and Nina Spencer, unaware that the Landers

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.150
have been murdered, try to sell the Reyburn
house.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:01:02.040
Peter goes inside the house, but Nina, who's
pregnant, doesn't.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.640
The curse attaches itself to Peter, who stabs
Nina in their kitchen before drowning himself

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:07.780
in their tub.

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:13.250
In 2005, Faith and William Matheson move into
the house so that Faith, who has cancer, can

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:15.120
be closer to her doctors.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.260
Both Faith and William see ghosts, but while
William isn't too worried, Faith loses her

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.260
mind.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:25.940
By the time Lorna Moody, an assisted suicide
attendant, comes by to help Faith die with

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.700
dignity, Faith is completely gone.

00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:31.960
Faith murders William and cuts off her own
fingers.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:36.560
Lorna flees, but sees a vision of Sam Landers
while driving and crashes her car.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.230
Her body isn't found for months.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:43.310
This is where Detective Muldoon enters the
picture.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.590
"Mrs. Matheson.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.350
I'm Detective Muldoon."

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:56.270
In 2006, Muldoon moves to town just a few
months after losing her husband, forcing her

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:58.000
to raise her son Burke alone.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:02.840
Her new partner, Detective Goodman, has a
few tragedies in his past, too.

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:08.080
His original partner, Wilson, became obsessed
with the house at 44 Reyburn Drive after investigating

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:10.840
the Landers killings, and eventually shot
himself.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.290
He survived, and is now institutionalized.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:17.299
Most importantly, however, Goodman isn't haunted
by the curse.

00:02:17.299 --> 00:02:22.430
See, he never stepped inside the Reyburn house,
it gave him a weird feeling, so he stayed

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:25.640
away and so he's free of its supernatural
tormentors.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.540
"Why'd you never go into that place?"

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.029
"Something never felt right about it."

00:02:31.029 --> 00:02:36.459
The original Grudge hinted at the idea and
its sequels made it explicit but the reboot

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:41.209
makes it clear: the ju-on, or "grudge," will
infect anyone who steps into the location

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:42.469
where the curse lives.

00:02:42.469 --> 00:02:45.709
Stay outside, and you're fine.

00:02:45.709 --> 00:02:49.430
Muldoon doesn't know this, though, so she
enters the house while investigating Lorna

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.749
Moody's death.

00:02:50.749 --> 00:02:53.840
Almost immediately, the Landers family begins
haunting her.

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:58.571
Afraid that the visions will make her hurt
Burke, Muldoon decides to burn the Reyburn

00:02:58.571 --> 00:03:01.950
house to the ground, hopefully ending the
curse.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.430
The house is destroyed, but as the final scene
shows, it doesn't do much.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:08.639
The Landers' spirits are still around.

00:03:08.639 --> 00:03:14.240
There's one big question that The Grudge doesn't
explicitly answer, and it's a big one: What

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:17.629
horrific act of violence created the curse?

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:21.049
The 2020 film begins with the curse already
active.

00:03:21.049 --> 00:03:23.620
Fiona has already been infected in the opening
scene.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:26.949
When she returns home, her family's death
is a foregone conclusion.

00:03:26.949 --> 00:03:33.559
To find the explanation, you actually need
to go back to the 2004 version of The Grudge.

00:03:33.559 --> 00:03:38.480
Yup, that's right: The Japanese house where
Fiona works in is the same one featured in

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.950
the Sarah Michelle Gellar flick that kicked
off the American leg of the franchise.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:48.470
In the 2004 movie, we discover that the curse
was born when Takeo Saeki learned that his

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:51.930
wife, Kayako, was in love with her college
professor.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:57.359
In a fit of jealousy, Takeo murdered Kayako
and their son, Toshio, creating the curse.

00:03:57.359 --> 00:04:00.489
The Grudge reboot doesn't spell this out,
but the clues are there.

00:04:00.489 --> 00:04:05.089
Perhaps the most telling one is that Detective
Wilson says that he's talked to a detective

00:04:05.089 --> 00:04:10.059
named Nakagawa, who investigated a murder
at the house where Fiona was working.

00:04:10.059 --> 00:04:13.359
That's the Japanese detective who appeared
in the original Grudge.

00:04:13.359 --> 00:04:18.150
The house in the opening scene also looks
a lot like the one in the 2004 movie, and

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:23.710
the film's end credits confirm that the ghost
Fiona sees in the garbage bag is indeed Kayako,

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.550
the antagonist of the first three Grudge movies.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:32.180
Given that the 2004 Grudge and the 2020 Grudge
stick to a similar formula, it's possible

00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:34.470
that the reboot's sequels will too.

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:37.360
If so, here's what you can expect.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:43.270
Like the 2020 version of The Grudge, The Grudge
2 takes place between 2004 and 2006.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:48.240
In the earlier timeline, Karen's sister, Aubrey,
travels to Japan to bring Karen home, and

00:04:48.240 --> 00:04:51.970
ends up infected by the curse and dying for
her efforts.

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:56.690
In the 2006 story, three girls break into
the Saeki house on a dare.

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:02.860
Two die, but another, haunted by Aubrey's
spirit and Kayako, returns to the United States,

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.740
bringing the curse to Chicago.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.979
In The Grudge 3, the sole surviving victim
from the previous movie dies, attracting the

00:05:08.979 --> 00:05:11.610
attention of Kayako's sister Naoko.

00:05:11.610 --> 00:05:17.860
Naoko moves to America and tries to exorcise
Takeo Saeki's spirit, hoping to end the curse

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:19.349
once and for all.

00:05:19.349 --> 00:05:21.009
The results are mixed.

00:05:21.009 --> 00:05:26.310
Naoko is killed during the process, and while
the exorcism is successful, Naoko's murder

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:31.020
sparks a whole new grudge, starting the process
all over again.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:35.650
On the other hand, the Grudge reboot introduces
enough new ideas to the mythology that a potential

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.220
sequel could go in a different direction.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:42.919
The revamp makes it clear that the curse can
spread not just from person to person but

00:05:42.919 --> 00:05:44.690
from location to location.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:49.960
The Saeki house might've been where it started,
but the Reyburn house ends up just as dangerous.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:54.979
If Muldoon's house is now another home base
for the curse, it wouldn't be too surprising.

00:05:54.979 --> 00:05:58.801
We don't know if Muldoon died at the end of
the movie or not, but the final shot of the

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:01.520
movie ominously lingers on her house.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.750
The house is filmed similarly to the Reyburn
house, too, with its street address number

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:08.629
14 featuring prominently in the frame.

00:06:08.629 --> 00:06:13.440
It could be that the Landers family relocated
to Muldoon's property when the Reyburn house

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:17.800
burned down, or maybe the town now has two
ghostly hotspots.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:22.919
Either way, if Burke asks your kid to stop
by for a sleepover, you should probably say

00:06:22.919 --> 00:06:24.310
no.

